The '''2025–26 Malaysia Super League''' ({{langx|ms|Liga Super Malaysia 2025–26}}) was the 22nd season of the [[Malaysia Super League]], the top-tier professional [[association football|football]] league in [[Malaysia]] since its establishment in 2004, and the 44th season of the top-flight [[Malaysian football league system|Malaysian football]] overall.

[[Johor Darul Ta'zim F.C.|Johor Darul Ta'zim]] are the defending champions, having won their record 12th Super League title in the previous season.<ref>{{cite web|url=https://stadiumastro.com/bola-sepak/terkini-liga-super-jdt-julang-kejuaraan-kali-ke11-berturutturut-283414 |title=TERKINI Liga Super: JDT julang kejuaraan kali ke-11 berturut-turut! |publisher=Stadium Astro |website=stadiumastro.com |date=24 February 2025 |access-date=25 February 2025 |first=Saufi |last=Tahir}}</ref>

==Teams==
===Changes from the previous season===
A total of thirteen teams contest the league, including ten from the [[2024–25 Malaysia Super League|2024–25 season]], two promoted from the [[2024–25 Malaysia A1 Semi-Pro League|A1 Semi-Pro League]] and one invited team. [[Kedah Darul Aman F.C.|Kedah Darul Aman]] and [[Perak F.C.|Perak]] were expelled following financial difficulties.<ref>{{Cite news|url=https://www.malaysianfootballleague.com/Content/Post/Watch/3714 |title=FIB Umum Keputusan Lesen Kebangsaan 2025-2026 |website=malaysianfootballleague.com |publisher=Malaysian Football League |access-date=22 May 2025 |date=22 May 2025}}</ref><ref>{{Cite news|url=https://stadiumastro.com/bola-sepak/selamat-tinggal-liga-super-perak-sahkan-tidak-mohon-pelesenan-kelab-288483 |title=Selamat tinggal Liga Super! Perak sahkan tidak mohon pelesenan kelab |website=stadiumastro.com |publisher=Stadium Astro |access-date=13 May 2025 |date=13 May 2025 |first=Muzaffar |last=Musa}}</ref> Two teams promoted from the A1 Semi-Pro League, [[Melaka F.C.|Melaka]] and [[Immigration F.C.|Immigration]], are debuting in the Super League.<ref name="MFL announcement">{{Cite news|url=https://files.malaysianfootballleague.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/06/DPMM-FC-CLUB-WILL-BOOST-THE-MALAYSIA-LEAGUE-COMPETITION-FOR-THE-2025-2028-SEASON.pdf |title=MFL Umum DPMM FC Sertai Liga Super, FFP Tetapkan Gaji Siling 80% & Keputusan Mesyuarat BOD KE-13 |website=malaysianfootballleague.com |publisher=Malaysian Football League |access-date=23 May 2025 |date=23 May 2025}}</ref><ref>{{Cite news|url=https://files.malaysianfootballleague.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/05/FIB-ANNOUNCES-NATIONAL-LICENSING-DECISIONS-1.docx |title=FIB Announces National Licensing Decisions for 2025–2026 |website=malaysianfootballleague.com |publisher=Malaysian Football League |access-date=23 May 2025 |date=22 May 2025}}</ref> Meanwhile, the [[Malaysian Football League]] (MFL) announced that the Brunei-based [[DPMM FC]] will compete in the new Super League season,<ref name="MFL announcement"/> after receiving approval from [[FIFA]] to participate in Malaysia’s professional league.<ref>{{Cite news|url=https://files.malaysianfootballleague.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/06/DPMM-FC-CLUB-WILL-BOOST-THE-MALAYSIA-LEAGUE-COMPETITION-FOR-THE-2025-2028-SEASON.pdf |title=DPMM FC Club will boost the Malaysia League Competition for The 2025–2028 season |website=malaysianfootballleague.com |publisher=Malaysian Football League |access-date=4 June 2025 |date=3 June 2025}}</ref> On 20 June, [[Sri Pahang F.C.|Sri Pahang]] have officially withdrawn from the 2025–26 season, despite being granted a national licence by the MFL.<ref>{{Cite news|url=https://www.malaysianfootballleague.com/Content/Post/Watch/3738 |title=13 Kelab Bakal Bersaing Dalam Liga Malaysia 2025–26 |website=malaysianfootballleague.com |publisher=Malaysian Football League |access-date=20 June 2025 |date=20 June 2025}}</ref> The club submitted a formal letter dated 16 June, stating their decision not to participate in the new campaign, which kicks off on 8 August 2025.<ref>{{Cite news|url=https://stadiumastro.com/bola-sepak/terkini-sri-pahang-sah-tarik-diri-hanya-13-pasukan-rebut-trofi-liga-super-202526-290912 |title=Sri Pahang sah tarik diri, hanya 13 pasukan rebut trofi Liga Super 2025/26 |website=stadiumastro.com |publisher=Stadium Astro |access-date=20 June 2025 |date=20 June 2025 |first=Saufi |last=Tahir}}</ref> Kelantan Darul Naim changed the name to [[Kelantan The Real Warriors F.C.|Kelantan The Real Warriors]] for this season.

